      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "James Sterling is the top choice because his Harvard MBA and reputation for an authoritative style directly align with the requirement for immediate command and gravitas in a boardroom setting. While Marcus Washington is personable and Arjun is analytically precise, both lack the specific polished, commanding communication style needed to instantly earn the respect of difficult Fortune 500 CEOs. Therefore, Sterling's track record in M&A and his established vocal presence make him the most qualified candidate for this high-stakes front-facing role.",
